+# Proof vs Monitor Policy (operator guidance)
+
+Purpose
+-------
+Help teams decide whether an invariant should be proved or monitored, and how to track outstanding items.
+
+Guidance (short)
+- Priority HIGH invariants: aim to prove. If proof not feasible within sprint, require monitored fallback with alerts and mitigation plan.
+- Priority MEDIUM: prefer proof, but monitoring acceptable if coverage demonstrated.
+- Priority LOW: monitoring and incident response acceptable.
+
+Process
+- Add invariants to ops/formal/invariant_registry_high_priority.json (for HIGH).
+- SME must provide SMT and meta with "sme_approved": true.
+- CI (ops/formal/proof_monitor.py) will detect missing proofs and emit /tmp/proof_monitor_report.json.
+- If missing_proof exists for HIGH:
+  - Create an issue, schedule SME sprint, attach counterexamples from prover CI.
+  - Until proof produced, implement runtime monitor and alerting; include mitigation in runbook.
+
+Acceptance
+- "Proved" state: proof artifact present (.proof.json) and indexed into evidence DB.
+- "Monitored" state: runtime monitor exists, alerts configured and drills executed monthly.
